rem ACMP 243 - Masquerade (Маскарад)
rem Solved in Euler 1-15 style with min-plus knapsack convolution and wholesale discount pricing.
rem
rem We need at least L meters of fabric from N shops. Each shop offers regular price P,
rem wholesale discount price Q for buying >= R meters, and stock limit F.
rem Buying more than L meters is allowed if it results in lower total cost.
rem
rem We compute each shop's piece-wise linear cost vector using vector arithmetic:
rem   DiscMask = (not (X less R)) integer
rem   Price = (Q * DiscMask) + (P * (1 - DiscMask))
rem   CostVec = concat (array 0) (X * Price)
rem
rem Then we transition DP via min-plus convolution:
rem   NextDP[M] = min_{0 <= X <= min(M, F)} (DP[M - X] + CostVec[X])
rem and take the minimum cost over target states M >= L.

use io
use cli
use sequences
use text
use numbers

arg N integer = 2
arg L integer = 14
arg ShopsText text = "7 9 6 10\n7 8 6 10"

INF = 1000000000

Tokens = (ShopsText words) integer
TotalStock = 0
for I in 0 till N
  F = Tokens (4 * I + 3)
  TotalStock = TotalStock + F
end

Answer = -1

if not (TotalStock less L)
  MaxCap = TotalStock min (L + 100)
  DP = array shape (MaxCap + 1) fill INF
  DP 0 = 0

  for I in 0 till N
    P = Tokens (4 * I)
    R = Tokens (4 * I + 1)
    Q = Tokens (4 * I + 2)
    F = Tokens (4 * I + 3)

    CostVec = array 0
    if F greater 0
      X = 1 to F
      DiscMask = (not (X less R)) integer
      Price = (Q * DiscMask) + (P * (1 - DiscMask))
      CostVec = concat (array 0) (X * Price)
    end

    NextDP = array shape (MaxCap + 1) fill INF
    for M in 0 to MaxCap
      LimitX = M min F
      X = 0 to LimitX
      PrevM = M - X
      Cand = (DP PrevM) + (CostVec X)
      NextDP M = Cand min
    end
    DP = NextDP
  end

  TargetSlice = DP (L to MaxCap)
  Answer = TargetSlice min
end

Answer print
